---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Changelog', url: '/changelog/' }];
---
<Base
  title="Inkline release notes and changelog | Inkline"
  description="What changed in each Inkline release, from 1.0 to the current version."
  path="/changelog/"
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <p class="kicker">Changelog</p>
  <h1>Release notes</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>1.4 <span class="dateline">July 2026</span></h2>
    <p>Inkline goes free to use. The free tier covers reading and the offline reader for up to 50 publications, notes, search, widgets and Voices; Inkline Pro gathers the monitoring toolkit: monitors, watchwords, spoken briefings, the written Brief and Compare Coverage analysis, and unlimited publications, from £2.99 a month with a week free. New in this release: Inkline Radio, a spoken briefing generated on the phone in a natural British voice; the Watch tab and watchwords for flagging clients, competitors and spokespeople; full article text in the reader for more sources; a customisable Today page; and Voices now lives at the top of Search.</p>
    <h2>1.3 <span class="dateline">July 2026</span></h2>
    <p>See how a story travels. The coverage view becomes a timeline: who broke a story, who followed and when, and whether it is one wire recycled or coverage genuinely gaining traction, with an on-device Apple Intelligence read of how the framing shifts as it spreads (on supported devices). New Home Screen and Lock Screen widgets: Latest, Coverage and Trending. Import your feeds from another reader with OPML, and start fresh anytime from Settings. Performance improvements throughout.</p>
    <h2>1.2: The Editorial Update <span class="dateline">July 2026</span></h2>
    <p>The publication directory arrives: 800+ sources across 50+ countries, hand-checked. Unified search across publications, desks and journalists. Voices rebuilt as a newsroom directory. "Also covered by" story comparison. Front Page becomes the default view, monitors made more reliable, and an editorial redesign drawn from the ink-and-ripple mark: the navy signature, the masthead, and a typography-first reader with three typefaces including OpenDyslexic.</p>
    <h2>1.1 <span class="dateline">July 2026</span></h2>
    <p>Inkline becomes a universal iPhone and iPad app. iPad adds a Today front page, a landscape reading workspace, handwritten Apple Pencil notes and desktop-class input with keyboard shortcuts, pointer and drag and drop. "Set up with AI" onboarding and a refreshed ink-drop identity across both devices.</p>
    <h2>1.0 <span class="dateline">14 July 2026</span></h2>
    <p>First release: verified sources, Apple Intelligence daily briefs, on-device summarisation, native article rendering, offline reading, widgets, Siri Shortcuts, a share extension and Spotlight indexing.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
